%! Module defaults and private predicates.
%!
%! A parameter of a module that @use leaves unbound takes its default.
%! The predicates a module derives for itself are private: a predicate
%! of the same name in the using program is another predicate.
%!
%! The example shows:
%! - how a module parameter falls back to its default,
%! - how the predicates of a module stay private to it.

% $limit is left out, so it is 3, the default in hops.rls:
@use hops { edge = road } as routes .

road(a, b) .
road(b, c) .
road(c, d) .
road(d, e) .

% Not the hops of the module, which is private to it:
hops(local, value, 0) .

reachable(?x, ?y) :- routes::within(?x, ?y) .
localHops(?x, ?y, ?n) :- hops(?x, ?y, ?n) .

@output reachable, localHops .
